speechtext:
This bill was introduced in the Senate and passed by that body. It is similar to the bill introduced in this house some time ago by the hon. member for South Timiskaming (Mr. Lang), to incorporate the Central Finance Corporation; this bill carries the same privileges and asks for the same rights. When the Central Finance Corporation bill was discussed in the Senate this bill was also considered, and they were both passed by that body. Special clauses were embodied in both these bills at the instance of the superintendent of insurance, Mr. Finlayson;

Private Bills
those clauses were submitted to the law clerks of the Senate and were approved by the committee and passed.
